Z||000004||Eric||05-14-2001||06:37 PM||||I drove a VW GTI 16V for awhile.  It was a nice quick car with a harsh ride similar to my modded 88's suspension.  However much I was impressed with the car, there's no way in hell my Fiero would lose to it.  I raced a new Civic Si too.  I killed him off the line.  By the time his Vtec kicked in, I was two or three lengths ahead.  He did, however, not lose any ground to me after 60mph or so.  Did I mention we were racing up a hill?  At the time I was driving with a clogged cat.  I think that's pretty much the same as a potato.  <P>Those cars were modded with something serious.  Do I smell nitrous?<p>[This message has been edited by Eric (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
