Z||000006||trigger||05-14-2001||06:42 PM||||There's nothing wrong with old VWs.  My friend has an Aztec 7 kit car which is built on a VW pan.  He has a 1600 cc VW motor bored out to 1850 cc, and a 4 speed VW transaxle.  The motor has forged pistons, aftermarket crank, better cam, and I think it has flowed heads.  He's also running a Buick Grand National turbo.  The car does 0-60 in under 4.5 seconds, and has an estimated top speed of 180 mph.  He already had it doing 140 at the top of third gear.  That car flies.  What really pisses me off about the whole deal is my 4 cyl auto 88 would beat him when he first bought the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
